   {
    "severity": "minor",
    "location": "formal/Ern/Corpus/MM3H.lean:761-775 (H49 docstring, \"New expected verdict (spec v0.1, by arbitration the obtained one)\")",
    "claim": "The docstring says the new endUse verdicts come \"by arbitration the obtained one\", but they do not. When Q21 fixed H49's regression verdict as \"verdict = verdict obtenu\", the obtained verdict was the v0 one: endUse 2 and endUse 3 ok, then reset reject, with 7 and 8 still active. The new verdict (endUse 2 and 3 reject) comes only from the v0.1 amendment of §69.2 (last sentence, the Q9 follow-up), which overrides the Q21 baseline. The verdict is correct and the clause is cited, so the change is not silent. Only the stated source is wrong: the text should say the v0.1 §69.2 amendment overrides the Q21 regression baseline, not that the verdict was taken from the obtained outcome, which the brief forbids.",
