   },
   {
    "severity": "minor",
    "location": "formal/Ern/Corpus/MM23H.lean:32-37 (module header) and :815-817 (MM23-H16 docstring)",
    "claim": "The rewritten docstrings say the lowest-address rule (a region with a leaf of nonzero size gets the lowest address among those leaves) is \"a decision of the reconstruction recorded for §82.3\". That rule came from the user's brief, and the HEAD text credited it to the brief. The new wording presents a user decision as an interpretation the reconstruction chose itself, which AGENTS.md forbids. MM23-H16 is the case that rests on this rule. Its verdict has no v0.1 source, and the header (lines 28-29) says such a case is 'kept with its expected verdict and classified', yet the file gives it no open-boundary or arbitration classification. The case itself passes.",
    "evidence": "git diff HEAD, MM23H.lean: removed `Address rules of references (decisions of the brief, recorded for §82.3 in Refinement.ptrAddr)` and, in H16, removed `a decision of the brief recorded for §82.3 (lowest-address rule)`; added `a decision of the reconstruction recorded for §82.3, not stated by v0.1` (lines 35-36) and `Source of the expected verdict: a decision of the reconstruction recorded for §82.3 (lowest-address rule), not stated by spec v0.1` (lines 815-816). Original brief, SP/brief.md:10: \"Decisions to apply: ... a region's pointer address is the lowest address among its non-empty leaves\". Spec v0.1 §82.2 decides only \"a region whose leaves all have zero physical size\". corpus-brief Q20/Q22 and arbitration Q22 classify MM23-H04, H09, H13, H14, H17 but not MM23-H16."
   },
   {
    "severity": "minor",
    "location": "formal/Ern/Corpus/MM3H.lean:25 and :37 (module header twin list)",
    "claim": "The header puts H16 in the list headed 'Twins that are not literally the same sequence without one faulty step', under 'a faulty element of several steps, removed: ... H16 (the `free`)'. H16's twin is exactly the run with one step removed: the single `free`. So the list misclassifies H16.",
    "evidence": "MM3H.lean:387 `def h16o := h16p ++ [.transfer 1 4, .free 3 7, .transfer 4 2, .exit]`; twin at :407 `Runs KF3 [] (h16p ++ [.transfer 1 4, .transfer 4 2, .exit, .read 3 [3]])`. Probe /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/ref/v01/review-corpus/MM3HProbe.lean (`lake env lean`, EXIT=0): `example : h16o ++ [.read 3 [3]] = h16p ++ [.transfer 1 4, .free 3 7, .transfer 4 2, .exit, .read 3 [3]] := rfl`. The two runs differ only by the one `.free 3 7` step."
   }
  ]
  Report: status, summary, changed, open (each rejected finding with its reason), and the final table of changed-verdict and mismatching cases for MM3H and MM23H.

